    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5505727/student-assistant-athletic-game-day-fan-experience-assistant-athletic-develo": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Athletic Game Day & Fan Experience Assistant (Athletic Development)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Athletic Game Day & Fan Experience Assistant (Athletic Development) Salary $10.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202700029 Org Athletic Development Opening Date 10/05/2026 Closing Date 2/28/2027 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Scott Allen Department Phone # (936) 468-3501 Department Email allends1@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 09/28/2026 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY Want to get behind the scenes of SFA Athletics? Love sports? Enjoy working with people? SFA Athletics is looking for an energetic, dependable SFA student to join our team and help create an incredible experience for our fans, donors, and guests. This is a hands-on, game-day position with a primary focus on home football games, premium seating, donor relations, and fan experience. On game days, it’s truly all hands on deck — so we're looking for someone who isn't afraid to roll up their sleeves and jump in wherever help is needed. This isn't a typical desk job. You'll get behind-the-scenes experience with SFA Athletics and see what it takes to put on a Division I college sporting event. You'll work alongside Athletics staff, interact with fans and donors, and gain valuable experience in event operations, hospitality, donor relations, and sports administration. If you're an SFA student who loves sports, enjoys being around people, and is ready to roll up your sleeves and be part of the team — we'd love to have you! JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student position responsible for assisting in the operations and activities of a department or a departmental project, program, or function. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Shows up, works hard, and can be counted on. Has a positive attitude and enjoys working with people. Willingness to jump in and help wherever needed. Ability to work in a fast-paced, sometimes unpredictable environment. Loves sports and is excited about SFA Athletics ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Helps set up and prepares for SFA home football games and other athletic events. Assists with premium seating, donor hospitality, and VIP areas. Helps with parking, signage, event setup, and game-day operations. Welcomes and assists fans, donors, season ticket holders, and guests. Helps create a fun, positive, and memorable game-day experience. Assists with event breakdown and cleanup after games. Supports Athletics staff with event planning, donor relations, and other projects when needed. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of general office and clerical procedures and concepts. Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records and files. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow instructions. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT This position will require a flexible schedule with the ability to work nights, weekends, holidays as sport. Most game-day shifts will begin a few hours before the game, except for football which typically starts several hours prior to kickoff, and continue through the completion of the game. Evening and weekend availability will be necessary for many home events. Additional hours may be available for office projects, event planning, and donor relations. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Why are you interested in working with SFA Athletics? 04 What do you enjoy most about sports, events, or being part of a team? 05 Tell us about a time when you had to work as part of a team to accomplish something. What was your role? 06 Game days can be busy and unpredictable. You may be asked to help with parking, set up an area, assist a fan, or move equipment — sometimes all within the same hour. How would you handle that? 07 This position involves interacting with donors, fans, season ticket holders, and other guests. How would you make sure someone has a positive experience when interacting with you? 08 Describe yourself in three words. Why did you choose those three words? 09 What do you hope to learn or gain from working with SFA Athletics? 10 Are you available to work evenings and weekends? 11 Are you available to work several hours before and through the completion of home football games? 12 Other availability or scheduling considerations: 13 You arrive for a football game and are told that the area you were assigned to help set up is already finished. Your supervisor asks you to help with something else, but you're not familiar with the task. What would you do? 14 I understand that this position requires dependability, a positive attitude, teamwork, flexibility, and a willingness to help wherever needed. I understand that game-day responsibilities may include working outdoors, being on my feet for extended periods, and assisting with setup and breakdown. No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5507194/lecturer-i-ii-or-iii-business-law": {
      "title": "Lecturer I, II, or III - Business Law",
      "description": "Lecturer I, II, or III - Business Law Location Main Campus Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202700035 Org Entrepreneurship and Applied Business Opening Date 10/06/2026 Closing Date 3/28/2027 11:59 PM Central FLSA Exempt Primary Contact Andrew Thornley Department Phone # (936) 468-1630 Department Email thornleyam@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 99 Projected Start Date 09/01/2027 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY The Rusche College of Business and the Schlief School of Accountancy seek to identify an outstanding faculty member in Business Law who demonstrates excellence in teaching, professional engagement, and service. The successful candidate will contribute to the delivery and continued development of the business law curriculum, support student success, and enhance the academic mission of the Rusche College of Business and the Schlief School of Accountancy. Particular consideration will be given to candidates with broad expertise in business law and related legal areas that support undergraduate and graduate business education. The successful candidate will help strengthen the college's reputation through high-quality instruction, meaningful engagement with students, and contributions to curricular and programmatic initiatives. Appointment may be made at the rank of Lecturer I, Lecturer II, or Lecturer III, depending on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and record of achievement. Minimum Qualifications Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an accredited institution. Licensed to practice law in a U.S. jurisdiction. Evidence of, or potential for, effective teaching Preferred Qualifications Master of Business Administration (MBA). Recent active practice of law. College-level teaching experience. JOB DESCRIPTION This is a full-time, nine-month, faculty position responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. Works under limited supervision, with moderate latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. Reports to the chair. QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in the field in which the individual will be teaching is required. Practical experience sufficient to teach at the university level, through teaching or profession, is required. Experience teaching at the university level is preferred. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs an equivalent of thirty teaching load credits (TLC) for the combined fall and spring semesters; reduction of teaching load through reassignment of duties is possible under certain circumstances. May conduct supplemental instructional activities such as independent studies, internships, and advising. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provides services to the university and the profession and engages in research/scholarly/creative activities. May supervise the work of student and/or graduate assistants. May serve on departmental, college, and university committees. Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge and practical experience in the field in which the individual will be teaching. Ability to effectively teach undergraduate and/or graduate students. Ability to work within a collaborative faculty environment. Ability to communicate effectively in both oral and written form. Ability to work effectively and patiently with students. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Safety Statement Stephen F. Austin State University recognizes the potential for accidents in performing job-related tasks. SFA promotes a safe working environment. Employees will be responsible for completing assigned tasks safely and efficiently. Employee evaluations will include safe job performance. This is a security-sensitive position subject to criminal record check. This is an IT-sensitive position subject to the Computer and Network Security policy. Sponsorship Statement In accordance with USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is eligible for participation in the Optional Retirement Program (ORP), subject to the position being full-time and at least 4 1/2 months in length, or the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) retirement plan, subject to the position being at least 20 hours per week and at least 135 days in length. For resources regarding retirement and benefits, navigate to the University of Texas System Employee Benefit page. Additional benefits for SFA employees are detailed on the SFA Benefits page. 01 Please select the highest level of education you have completed. Did not complete High School High school diploma or equivalent Some College Associate degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Doctorate degree or ABD 02 If you indicated that you have a degree, please list your field(s) of study. If you indicated ABD, please provide the expected date of degree completion. Enter N/A if this question does not apply. Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
