    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5445452/graduate-assistant-assessment-accountability-college-of-education": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Assessment & Accountability (College of Education)",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Assessment & Accountability (College of Education) Location Main Campus Job Type Graduate Assistant Job Number 202600641 Org EHSS Ed Prep Certification Opening Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date 12/15/2026 8:00 AM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Nikkie Strahan Department Phone # (936) 468-1064 Department Email strahanns@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 09/16/2026 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student position responsible for assisting faculty and/or staff with administrative duties, including gathering, organizing, and analyzing information related to the operations and activities of a department or a departmental project, program, or function. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a graduate student at Stephen F. Austin State University. The recommendation of a faculty member may be required. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provides office assistance to the department by assisting with administrative duties and responsibilities. Assists in collecting, verifying, compiling, monitoring, updating, tracking, and/or analyzing data related to the operations and activities of a department/assigned departmental program or function. Assists in promoting department services by providing faculty, staff, students, and/or the general public with applicable materials and information. Maintains and updates department records Assists in preparing, compiling, editing, updating, and disseminating various reports and documents. 6. Assists in responding to inquiries and providing ongoing support through e-mail, phone, and personal interaction. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of general office and clerical procedures and concepts. Skill in using computer applications including spreadsheet, database, and word processing software. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow instructions. Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records and files. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must have clear or provisional admission to the graduate school and the academic unit, be in good academic standing, and be enrolled for at least six semester credit hours (SCH) of graduate courses to be eligible for a graduate assistantship during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for a graduate assistantship during the summer, a student must be enrolled for at least three semester credit hours (SCH) of graduate courses. Graduate assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a student assistant, staff employee or adjunct faculty at the same time that they are employed as a graduate assistant. All graduate assistant appointments combined should not exceed the maximum FTE of 0.50. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is eligible for medical insurance coverage, subject to the position being appointed at 50% FTE for at least 4.5 months (135 calendar days). For resources regarding benefits for graduate assistants, navigate to the University of Texas System Employee Benefit page. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5474401/graduate-assistant-graduate-hall-director-residence-life": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Graduate Hall Director (Residence Life)",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Graduate Hall Director (Residence Life) Salary $550.00 Semi-Monthly Location Main Campus Job Type Graduate Assistant Job Number 202600669 Org Residence Life Operations Opening Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date 2/21/2027 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Andres Jaimes Department Phone # (936) 468-5103 Department Email ResLife@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 09/16/2026 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a live-in position responsible for maintaining a community environment within residence halls and promoting and enhancing students’ social, educational, and personal development. Responsible for articulating the philosophy and policies of the department and university. Works under moderate supervision, with limited latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. Reports to Residence Director. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a graduate student at Stephen F. Austin State University. The recommendation of a faculty member may be required. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Two or more years of prior experience living and working in a residence hall or similar group living environment is preferred. Must be in good standing with a minimum 3.0 GPA throughout period of employment. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Physical condition adequate to permit full performance of duties, including but not limited to the ability to detect smoke and other odors indicative of hall violations and hazardous situations and to climb stairs in order to reach the top floor of a residence hall in an emergency situation without assistance. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Interacts with students in assigned residence halls during duty and non-duty hours. Acts as a referral agent for students and staff to different campus and community resources. Assesses resident needs and coordinates with various university departments to meet their needs. Actively and collaboratively maintains a community environment that promotes respect, growth, academic success, and compassion. Maintains confidentiality of information as appropriate. Oversees the development and implementation of staff and student programming. Identifies potential hall leaders and directs their involvement at the floor and hall levels; facilitates their development. Responds to and communicates effectively in all emergency and/or life-threatening situations. Actively and appropriately addresses and documents all student conduct concerns. Ensures building security and safety. Prepares paperwork for and conducts student judicial hearings. Works closely with departmental maintenance and custodial staff to ensure a well-maintained environment and identifies facilities in need of repair or special attention. Coordinates periodic room inspections and proper check-in and check-out of residents. Assists in recruiting, selecting, training, supervising, and evaluating student staff members. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Supports and recruits for Residence Hall Association (RHA), Hall Council, and Honor Council meetings. Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of, or the ability to learn, departmental and university policies and procedures. Knowledge of student development theory, techniques, and research associated with ensuring the success of various student populations. Skill in the use of standard office equipment and software. Ability to communicate effectively in both oral and written form. Ability to exercise sound judgment in making decisions. Ability to diffuse and respond effectively to situations involving intense pressures and/or unpredictable persons. Ability to react quickly and calmly in emergency situations. Ability to provide support for student development with a demonstrable concern for students. Ability to engage students and to create and enhance their connection to the institution and each other. Ability to establish and maintain a good rapport with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to train and supervise others. Ability to live and work on campus in order to respond to the needs of the department 24 hours per day. Ability to observe and detect unusual occurrences and policy violations. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT BENEFITS: • Compensation : Monthly stipend of $1,100 per month. ( NOTE : This may interfere with your financial aid package, so be sure to communicate with the Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships if applicable.) • Living Accommodations : On-campus furnished apartment including utilities, washer & dryer, and high-speed internet access; pets are allowed according to policy. • Scholarship : Tuition and fee scholarship (in-state rate) of up to $10,000 to cover up to 9 hours per fall and spring semesters. Student meal plan scholarship (approximately $1,500 per semester, fall and spring semesters). SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must have clear or provisional admission to the graduate school and the academic unit, be in good academic standing, and be enrolled for at least six semester credit hours (SCH) of graduate courses to be eligible for a graduate assistantship during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for a graduate assistantship during the summer, a student must be enrolled for at least three semester credit hours (SCH) of graduate courses. Graduate assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a student assistant, staff employee or adjunct faculty at the same time that they are employed as a graduate assistant. All graduate assistant appointments combined should not exceed the maximum FTE of 0.50. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is eligible for medical insurance coverage, subject to the position being appointed at 50% FTE for at least 4.5 months (135 calendar days). For resources regarding benefits for graduate assistants, navigate to the University of Texas System Employee Benefit page. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Have you been admitted to SFA’s graduate program? No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5474451/student-assistant-work-study-football-equipment-manager-football-operations": {
      "title": "Student Assistant (Work Study) - Football Equipment Manager (Football Operations)",
      "description": "Student Assistant (Work Study) - Football Equipment Manager (Football Operations) Salary $10.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Work Study) Job Number 202700012 Org Football Operations Opening Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date 1/8/2027 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Derek Whoolery Department Phone # (936) 468-3501 Department Email Derek.Whoolery@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a work-study student position responsible for assisting in the maintenance, issuance, collection, inspection, repair and replacement of football equipment and the upkeep of equipment-related facilities. Works under close supervision, with minimal latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. A student must be awarded and accept a “Work-Study Permit” for each semester the student will be working. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Performs repetitive manual work for various physically demanding tasks, including lifting, sorting, organizing, and carrying equipment, loading and unloading vehicles, standing and walking for extended periods of time. Position also requires the ability to work outdoors in exposure to various weather conditions. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Manages the issuance, collection, maintenance, repair, and replacement of football equipment for student-athletes, coaches, and staff. Maintains accurate equipment inventory records and tracks equipment assignments to student-athletes. Conducts equipment fittings and ensures proper sizing, adjustment, and safety of protective equipment. Maintains equipment rooms, locker rooms, storage areas, and related facilities in a clean, organized, and functional condition. Monitors equipment condition, removes damaged or unsafe items from service, and coordinates repairs or warranty claims as needed. Prepares, distributes, and manages equipment required for daily football practices, workouts, and team activities. Assists with home game operations, including field setup, sideline preparation, equipment distribution, and postgame breakdown. Prepares, packs, transports, loads, and unloads equipment for team travel and coordinates equipment needs for away contests. Maintains professional working relationships and collaborates with football staff and other athletics departments to support program operations. Supports football operations and performs other related duties as assigned to meet the needs of the football program. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of, or ability to learn, football equipment operations and industry standards. Skill in organizing, maintaining, and tracking equipment inventory. Skill in completing assignments accurately and with attention to detail. Ability to communicate effectively in oral and written form. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with student-athletes, coaches, staff, vendors, and campus personnel. Ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT This position requires a flexible schedule based on the football program's operational needs. Work hours may include: early mornings, evenings, weekends, holidays, home football games, away-game travel, preseason camp, postseason competition, and football camps and clinics. Extended hours should be expected during the football season and other high-demand periods. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Student must have received a work-study award. Please reach out to Financial Aid to confirm your eligibility for work-study before you apply. A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Are you eligible for Federal or State Work Study? No Yes Not sure 04 Are you able to work a flexible schedule based on the football program's operational needs, including extended hours during the football season and other high-demand periods? No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5475145/graduate-assistant-development-and-donor-relations-assistant-intercollegiate-a": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Development and Donor Relations Assistant (Intercollegiate Athletics)",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Development and Donor Relations Assistant (Intercollegiate Athletics) Salary $24,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus Job Type Graduate Assistant Job Number 202700011 Org Intercollegiate Athletics Opening Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date 3/8/2027 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Scott Allen Department Phone # (936) 468-3501 Department Email allends1@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 10/01/2026 Position End Date (for temp assignments) 08/31/2027 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION Want to build real-world experience in collegiate athletics while helping connect SFA Athletics with its donors, fans, and supporters? SFA Athletics is looking for an energetic, organized, and relationship-focused Graduate Assistant to join our team and play an important role in the planning and execution of athletic events and donor engagement initiatives. This position will work closely with Athletics development staff and will have a particular focus on donor relations, donor events, premium seating, fan experience, and game-day operations. The Graduate Assistant will have opportunities to take ownership of projects while gaining valuable experience in the day-to-day operation of a Division I athletics development department. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a graduate student at Stephen F. Austin State University. The recommendation of a faculty member may be required. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Must be enrolled in a graduate program at SFA. Previous experience experience in athletics, fundraising, development, events, hospitality, or customer service is preferred, but a willingness to learn and work hard is just as important. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Assists with the planning, coordination, and execution of donor events and hospitality experiences. Takes an active role in preparing event timelines, guest lists, materials, signage, and other event details. Serves as a welcoming and professional representative of SFA Athletics at donor events. Assists development staff with donor communications and outreach, including invitations, event communications, thank-you messages, and other correspondence. Supports donor stewardship and engagement initiatives. Assists with maintaining accurate records and organizing donor-related information. Provides administrative and project support to the Athletics development team. Assists with planning and execution of SFA home athletic events, with an emphasis on football. Helps oversee premium seating and donor hospitality areas. Assists with parking, event setup, signage, guest services, and pre-game setup, as well as in-game responsibilities, and post-game breakdown Interacts directly with donors, fans, season ticket holders, VIPs, and other guests to develop meaningful face-to-face relationships. Helps troubleshoot issues and ensures guests receive a memorable first-class experience. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of collegiate athletics, development, fundraising, event management, or hospitality. Skill in building relationships and interacting with people. Ability to be detail-oriented and organized while keeping a positive attitude in a fast-paced environment. Ability to be comfortable communicating with donors and other high-level guests. Ability to manage multiple products and deadlines. Ability to work successfully as a member of a team, and maintain a positive attitude. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT Schedule will vary based on the athletic calendar and department needs. Game-day responsibilities will generally begin several hours before kickoff and continue through the completion of the game, with additional responsibilities following the event as needed. The position may also include regular office hours for event planning, donor communications, development projects, and administrative support. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Safety Statement A student must have clear or provisional admission to the graduate school and the academic unit, be in good academic standing, and be enrolled for at least six semester credit hours (SCH) of graduate courses to be eligible for a graduate assistantship during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for a graduate assistantship during the summer, a student must be enrolled for at least three semester credit hours (SCH) of graduate courses. Graduate assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a student assistant, staff employee or adjunct faculty at the same time that they are employed as a graduate assistant. All graduate assistant appointments combined should not exceed the maximum FTE of 0.50. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is eligible for medical insurance coverage, subject to the position being appointed at 50% FTE for at least 4.5 months (135 calendar days). For resources regarding benefits for graduate assistants, navigate to the University of Texas System Employee Benefit page. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
