      "title": "Student Assistant - Office Assistant (Post Office)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Office Assistant (Post Office) Salary $7.25 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202600627 Org Post Office Opening Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date 12/31/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Bobbie Stewart Department Phone # (936) 468-2307 Department Email bobbie.stewart@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 08/17/2026 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student position responsible for assisting in the operations and activities of a department or a departmental project, program, or function. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provides office assistance to the department by assisting staff in routine clerical duties and responsibilities. Provides assistance in answering phone calls, routing incoming calls, taking messages, greeting visitors, and directing visitors to appropriate staff member. Assists in file and records maintenance. Assists in the preparation and implementation of departmental project/program activities. Provides general information and/or training regarding project/program. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of general office and clerical procedures and concepts. Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records and files. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow instructions. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5443229/student-assistant-work-study-career-advocate-center-for-career-education-and": {
      "title": "Student Assistant (Work Study) - Career Advocate (Center for Career Education and Exploration)",
      "description": "Student Assistant (Work Study) - Career Advocate (Center for Career Education and Exploration) Salary $8.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Work Study) Job Number 202600618 Org Career Center Opening Date 08/10/2026 Closing Date 12/10/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact April Place Department Phone # (936) 468-3305 Department Email april.place@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 08/17/2026 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION Student Career Advocates (SCAs) assist in the daily operations of the Center for Career Education and Exploration. SCAs connect with fellow students to help them grow professionally. SCAs lead presentations, meet with students, edit documents such as resumes and cover letters, interact with employers looking to hire SFA students and more. This is a federal work-study student position. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. A student must be awarded and accept a “Work-Study Permit” for the semester. Maintain an overall GPA of 2.5 or higher and must be in good standing with the university. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Strong customer service attitude and experience Presentation or teaching experience Desire to help others ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provides office assistance to the department by completing routine clerical duties and responsibilities. Responds to various internal and external inquiries by managing emails, multi-line phone system, and in-person requests. Provides clear and effective customer service and communication with a variety of audiences. Assists in the preparation, marketing and implementation of departmental programs and activities including special events, workshops, resource tables, presentations, Career Closet, and other activities as needed. Receives training on and completes professional document critiques and edits through online submissions and in-person appointments. Manages Handshake, an online career platform, for student, employer and departmental accounts. Helps coordinate, prepare and execute career fairs. Leads presentations on student professional development. Works in a team environment to accomplish departmental goals and expectations. Completes required trainings as assigned. Performs other related duties as assigned. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of professional telephone and email etiquette. Knowledge of general office and clerical procedures and concepts. Skill in the use of standard office equipment and software. Ability to communicate effectively in both oral and written form. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow procedures and directions. Ability to work independently and collectively. Ability to demonstrate initiative and accomplish goals and expectations. Ability to manage multiple tasks, problem solve, be flexible and learn quickly. Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records and files. Ability to demonstrate maturity, trustworthiness, responsibility, motivation, cheerfulness, and dependability as a worker. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT Student must have received a work-study award. Please reach out to Financial Aid to confirm your eligibility for work-study before you apply. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Do you have an overall GPA of 2.5 or higher and are you in good standing with the university? No Yes 04 Are you eligible for Federal or State Work Study? No Yes Not sure 05 When are you available to start work? Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
