    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5458775/student-assistant-photo-lab-assistant-school-of-art": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Photo Lab Assistant (School of Art)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Photo Lab Assistant (School of Art) Salary $10.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202600672 Org Art Opening Date 08/24/2026 Closing Date 10/31/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Kendra McMullan Department Phone # (936) 468-2934 Department Email kendra.mcmullan@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 09/14/2026 Position End Date (for temp assignments) 05/14/2027 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student position responsible for assisting in the operations and activities of a department or a departmental project, program, or function. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. Must be a Photography major and have taken ARTS 2356. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Must be available for the majority of the photography darkroom class period: Tuesday and Thursday, 11:00 AM to 1:40 PM. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provides office assistance to the department by assisting staff in routine clerical duties and responsibilities. Provides assistance in answering phone calls, routing incoming calls, taking messages, greeting visitors, and directing visitors to appropriate staff member. Assists in file and records maintenance. Assists in the preparation and implementation of departmental project/program activities. Provides general information and/or training regarding project/program. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of general office and clerical procedures and concepts. Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records and files. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow instructions. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Are you a photography major and have taken ARTS 2356? No Yes 04 Are you available to work the photography dark room class period, Tuesday and Thursday, 11:00 AM to 1:40 PM? No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5459992/student-assistant-art-gallery-assistant-school-of-art": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Art Gallery Assistant (School of Art)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Art Gallery Assistant (School of Art) Salary $9.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202600679 Org Art Opening Date 08/25/2026 Closing Date 11/1/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Kendra McMullan Department Phone # (936) 468-2934 Department Email kendra.mcmullan@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 09/04/2026 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student position responsible for assisting in the operations and activities of a department or a departmental project, program, or function. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provides office assistance to the department by assisting staff in routine clerical duties and responsibilities. Provides assistance in answering phone calls, routing incoming calls, taking messages, greeting visitors, and directing visitors to appropriate staff member. Assists in file and records maintenance. Assists in the preparation and implementation of departmental project/program activities. Provides general information and/or training regarding project/program. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of general office and clerical procedures and concepts. Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records and files. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow instructions. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT While the Adams Gallery is located on the main SFA campus, this position may require you to commute to the SFA Cole Art Center galleries located in Downtown Nacogdoches. This position may require you to work weekends or occasionally evenings for events. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 While the Adams Gallery is located on the main SFA campus, this position may require you to commute to the SFA Cole Art Center galleries located in Downtown Nacogdoches. Please answer if that would not be possible for you, and if you would only be able to work on the main campus. No - I am only able to work on the main campus. Yes - I am able to commute to the SFA Cole Art Center galleries located in Downtown Nacogdoches. Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5401425/student-assistant-work-study-hr-information-system-hris-assistant-human-re": {
      "title": "Student Assistant (Work Study) - HR Information System (HRIS) Assistant (Human Resources)",
      "description": "Student Assistant (Work Study) - HR Information System (HRIS) Assistant (Human Resources) Salary $8.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Work Study) Job Number 202600566 Org Human Resources Opening Date 07/07/2026 Closing Date 11/7/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Kim Odems Department Phone # (936) 468-2304 Department Email hr@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a work-study student position responsible for assisting in the operations and activities of the Human Resources Information System ( HRIS ) team within the Human Resources department. Works under close supervision, with minimal latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Familiarity with Banner or other HRIS is preferred. Interest in HR data management is preferred. A student must be awarded and accept a “Work-Study Permit” for each semester the student will be working. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Assists HRIS team with routine data entry, data cleaning and general data management tasks within the Human Resource Information System ( HRIS ) to ensure data accuracy and integrity. Supports the maintenance and updating of HRIS records. Reviews and updates data entries to identify and correct discrepancies or errors. Assists with answering phone calls and routing incoming calls, and provides general information to customers regarding HRIS processes and procedures. Ensures confidentiality and follows data privacy policies when handling sensitive HR information. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of, or the ability to learn, university and departmental policies and procedures. Knowledge of basic data entry concepts. Skill in completing assignments with attention to detail. Skill in computer applications including spreadsheet, database, and word processing software. Ability to accurately enter, update, and maintain HR data within the HRIS . Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and professionalism. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow instructions. Ability to organize work. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT This position is 15-20 hours/week scheduled between 8:00 AM-5:00 PM Monday-Friday in the office (Austin Building 201) SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Student must have received a work-study award. Please reach out to Financial Aid to confirm your eligibility for work-study before you apply. A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Are you eligible for Federal or State Work Study? No Yes Not sure 04 Do you have experience in the use of computer software (word processing, database, and spreadsheet applications)? No Yes 05 Do you have experience working with confidential information? No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5410240/student-assistant-advertising-agency-assistant-center-of-applied-research-and": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Advertising Agency Assistant (Center of Applied Research and Rural Innovation)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Advertising Agency Assistant (Center of Applied Research and Rural Innovation) Salary $15.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202600578 Org N-FS Cntr Applied Rsrch Rural Innov Opening Date 07/14/2026 Closing Date 11/14/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Trisha Wheeler Department Phone # (936) 468-1234 Department Email trisha.wheeler@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 08/03/2026 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student assistant position responsible for assisting in the Advertising Agency Team. We are seeking motivated student workers who are seeking to gain real-world experience in advertising, marketing and creative communications. Students will work on client projects while receiving professional guidance and mentorship to build portfolios and experience in preparation for future careers. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Assists with campaign strategy, planning, content creation, graphic design, research, client communication, and event promotion based on their assigned role. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual is preferred to possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities. Applicants are not expected to have every skill listed below. Students will be assigned roles based on their strengths, interests and areas they would like to develop. Knowledge of social media platforms, content strategies, and digital marketing best practices. Knowledge of graphic design, multimedia production, and content creation tools. Knowledge of marketing, branding, and audience engagement principles. Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication. Skill in creative content development, copywriting, and storytelling. Skill in effective organization, time management, and project coordination. Ability to create engaging digital content for diverse audiences. Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to collaborate effectively, learn quickly, and contribute innovative ideas. Ability to maintain a sense of fun and willingness to take risks. Zigging while everybody else zags. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT Please include portfolio or examples of work in documents sections labeled \"other\". Start dates are flexible. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Which client area are you most interested in working with? Fine Arts Athletics Both No preference 04 Which agency roles or areas of work interest you most? Select all that apply. Brand or account management Marketing strategy and audience research Copywriting and content creation Graphic design and art direction Photography, videography or video editing Social media and event promotion Open to exploring multiple roles Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
