    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5527457/student-assistant-desk-assistant-residence-life": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Desk Assistant (Residence Life)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Desk Assistant (Residence Life) Salary $9.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202700063 Org Residence Life Operations Opening Date 10/23/2026 Closing Date 11/2/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Andres Jaimes Department Phone # (936) 468-2601 Department Email reslife@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 01/04/2027 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student position responsible for working with residence hall staff to maintain the front desk operations in assigned housing facilities. Responsible for providing operational services to students, reporting concerns to residence hall and operations staff, and providing quality customer service to students while acting as a representative of SFA and the Residence Life Department. Works under close supervision, with limited latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Must be an active student in good academic standing (cumulative GPA of 2.3 or higher for undergraduate students or 3.0 or higher for graduate students). PHYSICAL DEMANDS Physical condition adequate to permit full performance of duties. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Understands, supports, follows, enforces, and educates students and staff about university objectives, policies, regulations, and Residence Life Community Guidelines. Maintains ongoing communication with departmental staff. Displays a positive, professional attitude and support towards students, staff, and the department. Works the residence hall front desk at least 16 hours per week . Actively and appropriately addresses and informs hall staff of all student conduct concerns. Makes self available and accessible to students while at desk. Acts as a referral agent for students and staff to different campus and community resources. Keeps residents and staff informed of activities. Attends and participates in all staff training sessions, including weekly staff meetings, in-service training sessions, and others as assigned. Completes administrative duties and paperwork associated with desk operations. Ensures building security and safety. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of, or the ability to learn, university and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to understand and follow instructions. Ability to maintain effective interpersonal relationships. Ability to complete work accurately and in a timely manner. Ability to respond quickly and appropriately to emergencies. Ability to handle stressful situations and display mature judgment. Ability to work effectively and patiently with students. Ability to work with and maintain confidential information. Ability to work extended hours including evenings, nights, and weekends as assigned. Also required to return approximately 8 days before beginning of each term and remain until after halls have closed for each semester. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT Desk Assistants are required to return approximately 8 days before beginning of each term and remain until after halls have closed for each semester. Desk Assistants can only work 6.5 hours/week in any other SFA or on-campus job. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 How many hours are you enrolled in during the current semester? 04 How many college credit hours have you completed? 05 When do you expect to graduate? Please provide semester and year. 06 Do you have a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.3 as an undergraduate student or 3.0 as a graduate student? No Yes 07 Have you lived in on-campus housing for at least 2 semesters? No Yes 08 Please provide the following information: Current Residence Hall, Current Room, Current Address/SFASU Mail Box, City, State, Zip Code. Preference will be given to a candidate with a residence hall assignment, but it is not required. Please type N/A if you do not wish to disclose. 09 What is your mySFA email address? ALL communication will be done through your SFASU email account. 10 Have you ever been subject to disciplinary action as a result of a violation of the Community Guidelines, Student Code of Conduct, or University Policy? PLEASE NOTE: Prior involvement with the Office of Student Conduct does not automatically exclude you from consideration. No Yes 11 If yes, please explain what you learned from this experience. If no, please type N/A in the text box. 12 The mission of Residence Life is to provide a learner-centered residential environment which is conducive to the academic success and personal development of our students. The Desk Assistant's main responsibility is to support Residence Life in attaining its goals for the residents. Tell us about yourself and how you will contribute as a Desk Assistant in supporting this mission. (250 - 500 words). 13 I understand to be a Desk Assistant, I must a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.3 as an undergraduate student or 3.0 as a graduate student and be in good standing. To this end, I authorize Residence Life to access my academic and student conduct record for any potential or sustained employment matters. No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5527544/student-assistant-residence-hall-association-executive-board-residence-life": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Residence Hall Association Executive Board (Residence Life)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Residence Hall Association Executive Board (Residence Life) Salary $300.00 Monthly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202700066 Org RHA Programs Opening Date 10/23/2026 Closing Date 11/7/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Emilee Cude Department Phone # (936) 968-2601 Department Email rha@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 01/04/2027 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a student position responsible for planning and executing cross campus, large-scale programming. Assists with departmental projects, functions, and programs as needed. The Residence Hall Association (RHA) Executive Board consists of the President, Vice President, Hall Council Coordinator, Secretary, Marketing Coordinator, and National Communications Coordinator. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provides support and assistance to Hall Council members Assists in the planning, preparation, and execution of RHA programs and events Assists in the planning, preparation, and execution of departmental programs Maintains records and files related to the operation and activities of the Residence Hall Association NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Ability to plan and organize events. Ability to properly maintain records and files. Ability to communicate professionally with peers and supervisors. Ability to follow instructions. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT RHA Executive Board members are expected to work in the RHA Office for a minimum of 10 hours each week, to be active in programming, and to attend a weekly RHA meeting. These positions are paid monthly and are scheduled to start January 4, 2026. Applicants may upload one or more letters of recommendation as an optional document. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 What RHA Executive Board position(s) are you interested (mark all that apply)? President Vice President Hall Council Coordinator Secretary Marketing Coordinator National Communications Coordinator 04 What interests you in a leadership position with RHA? 05 What experience do you have in leadership or student engagement roles? How would you describe your leadership style? 06 If hired, what are some ideas you would implement to expand the positive impact of the RHA on SFA students? 07 Describe a time when you handled a challenging situation when time pressures were a factor. What was the outcome? 08 RHA Executive Board members are expected to work in the RHA Office for a minimum of 10 hours each week, to be active in programming, and to attend a weekly RHA meeting. How do you plan to balance RHA obligations with your school work and everyday responsibilities? 09 As an RHA Executive Board member, you are the voice of the residents. Describe a time when you advocated for something in which you believed. Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5527583/student-assistant-resident-assistant-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Resident Assistant (Spring 2027)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Resident Assistant (Spring 2027) Salary $50.00 Monthly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202700061 Org Residence Life Operations Opening Date 10/23/2026 Closing Date 11/2/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Andres Jaimes Department Phone # (936) 468-2601 Department Email reslife@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 01/04/2027 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION This is a live-in student position responsible for facilitating the social, educational, and intellectual development of each student through developing a community within SFA's residence halls. Responsible for articulating the philosophy and policies of the Residence Life Department and SFA to residents while representing the department as a role model in all facets of university life. This position is assigned to floors/areas of approximately 25 to 55 students. Works under close supervision, with limited latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. Must be an active student in good academic standing (cumulative GPA of 2.3 or higher for undergraduate students or 3.0 or higher for graduate students). No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Two semesters of residence hall living, Hall Council experience or participation, and/or related experience is preferred. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Physical condition adequate to permit full performance of duties. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Understands, supports, follows, enforces, and educates students and staff about university objectives, policies, and regulations and Residence Life Community Guidelines. Maintains ongoing communication with departmental staff. Displays a positive, professional attitude and support towards students, staff, and the department. Works the residence hall front desk six hours each week. Participates in weekday and weekend residence hall duty rotation. Makes oneself available and accessible to students by proactively interacting with residents in designated residence halls during duty and non-duty hours. Acts as a referral agent for students and staff to different campus and community resources. Attends, participates in, supports, and recruits for Residence Hall Association (RHA), Hall Councils, and other associations. Keeps residents and staff informed of campus activities. Attends and participates in all staff training sessions, including weekly staff meetings, in-service training sessions, and others as assigned. Assists in coordinating the programming needs and assessment process in assigned halls. Actively and appropriately addresses and documents all student conduct and community guidelines concerns. Ensures building security and safety. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of, or the ability to learn, university and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to understand and follow instructions. Ability to maintain effective interpersonal relationships. Ability to complete work accurately and in a timely manner. Ability to respond quickly and appropriately to emergencies. Ability to handle stressful situations and display mature judgment. Ability to work effectively and patiently with students. Ability to work with and maintain confidential information. Ability to work extended hours including evenings, nights, and weekends as assigned. Also required to return approximately 8 days before beginning of each term and remain until after halls have closed for each semester. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT This position is for Spring 2027. BENEFITS: • Compensation : Monthly stipend of $50. • Living Accommodations : Individual room, as long as capacity allows. NOTE: Resident Assistants are required to return approximately 8 days before the beginning of each term and remain until after the halls have closed for each semester. Resident Assistants can only work 6.5 hours/week in any other SFA or on-campus job. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major/minor? 03 Do you have a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.3 as an undergraduate student or 3.0 as a graduate student? No Yes 04 How many hours are you enrolled in during the current semester? 05 How many college credit hours have you completed? 06 When do you expect to graduate? Please provide semester and year. 07 Have you lived in on-campus housing for at least 2 semesters? No Yes 08 Please provide the following information: Current Residence Hall, Current Room, Current Address/SFASU Mail Box, City, State, Zip Code. Preference will be given to a candidate with a residence hall assignment, but it is not required. Please type N/A if you do not wish to disclose. 09 What is your mySFA email address? ALL communication will be done through your SFASU email account. 10 Please describe your involvement in Residence Life Organizations (RHA, Hall Council, NRHH, Welcome Jacks, etc.). 11 What leadership positions have you held outside Residence Life in the last 3 years? 12 Have you ever been subject to disciplinary action as a result of a violation of the Community Guidelines, Student Code of Conduct, or University Policy? PLEASE NOTE: Prior involvement with the Office of Student Conduct does not automatically exclude you from consideration. No Yes 13 If yes, please explain what you learned from this experience. If no, please type N/A in the text box. 14 The mission of Residence Life is to provide a learner-centered residential environment which is conducive to the academic success and personal development of our students. The Resident Assistant's main responsibility is to support Residence Life in attaining its goals for the residents. Tell us about yourself and how you will contribute as a Resident Assistant in supporting this mission. (250 - 500 words). 15 I understand to be a Resident Assistant, I must have a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.3 as an undergraduate student or 3.0 as a graduate student and be in good standing. To this end, I authorize Residence Life to access my academic and student conduct record for any potential or sustained employment matters. No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
    },
