    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sfasu/jobs/5535956/student-assistant-marleta-chadwick-financial-advisor-economics-and-finance": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Marleta Chadwick Financial Advisor (Economics and Finance)",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Marleta Chadwick Financial Advisor (Economics and Finance) Salary $12.00 Hourly Location Main Campus Job Type Student (Non-Work Study) Job Number 202700071 Org Economics and Finance Opening Date 10/30/2026 Closing Date 11/9/2026 11:59 PM Central FLSA Non-Exempt Primary Contact Dr. Matthew Jaramillo Department Phone # (936) 468-1783 Department Email Matthew.Jaramillo@sfasu.edu Salary Grade 0 Projected Start Date 01/10/2027 Description Benefits Questions SUMMARY JOB DESCRIPTION The Marleta Chadwick Student Financial Advisor supports peers by providing guidance on budgeting, saving, credit management, and responsible financial decision-making. This role focuses on helping students build practical money skills through one-on-one support, workshops, and resource sharing. This role helps students develop lifelong financial skills, reduce financial stress, and make informed decisions about their money. QUALIFICATIONS The minimum education required for admittance as a student at Stephen F. Austin State University. Enrollment as a full-time student is required. Must have basic understanding of personal finance principles. Completion of FINC 3369 is preferred. Academic financial planning concentration declaration is preferred. No direct experience is required. Training and instruction will be provided. Experience using budgeting tools or apps is preferred. Experience in public speaking or workshop facilitation is preferred. Experience in leadership or peer mentoring background is preferred. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Offers peer-to-peer guidance on budgeting, saving, and basic financial planning. Educates students on topics such as credit scores, debt management, and student loans. Assists students in creating personalized budgets and financial goals. Leads workshops, presentations, or group discussions on financial literacy topics. Shares reliable financial resources and tools with students. Maintains confidentiality and professionalism when discussing personal finances. Stays informed on current financial trends, tools, and student-related financial issues. NON-ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Performs other related duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The individual must possess the following knowledge, skills, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that the individual can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Knowledge of general office and clerical procedures and concepts. Ability to maintain effective interpersonal relationships. Ability to explain financial concepts in simple, relatable terms. Ability to process and handle confidential information with discretion. Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records and files. Ability to communicate professionally and courteously with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to understand and follow instructions. SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT A student must be enrolled in six or more semester hours to be eligible for student employment during the fall or spring semesters. To be eligible for student employment during the summer, a student must be enrolled in three or more semester hours or be registered for courses in the upcoming fall semester. Student assistants may not hold any other type of position such as a graduate assistantship or temporary casual employment at the same time that they are employed as a student assistant. SFA's breathtaking campus is located in the heart of East Texas in historic Nacogdoches . Did you know that if you live in the Houston or Dallas areas, Nacogdoches may actually be closer than Austin? It's true! SFA's salary grade table can be found in the pay grade structure section on the HR Manager's page . Stephen F. Austin State University, an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer and Educator, is committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, creed, color, age, national origin, religion or physical or mental disability as required by law. If, because of an impairment or disability, you need accommodation during any part of the employment process, please contact Human Resources at 936-468-2304 . Stephen F. Austin State University (SFA) is committed to providing a safe environment for its students and the broader campus community. SFA's police department actively works to prevent and respond to criminal activity through various measures, including comprehensive reporting practices and emergency alert systems.The university's Annual Fire and Safety Security Report details on-campus crime statistics, including incidents of forcible sex offenses, burglary, motor vehicle theft, and aggravated assault. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Which of the following best represents your current student classification? Entering Freshman Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student 02 What is your major? 03 Have you completed FINC 3369 or a comparable course? No Yes Required Question Employer Stephen F. Austin State University (TX) Address 1936 North St Nacogdoches, Texas, 75962 Phone 936-468-2304 Website https://www.sfasu.edu Apply"
